\\\"was derived from some of this work on upper-body non-impact plyometrics\\\", the research \\\"conducted in this field by the author in 1994\\\" (PDF p. 292 / printed p. 281), and gives no subject numbers or publication for it.\")\nrep('heuristic--maximal-plyometric-and-depth-jump-volume-and-rest.md',\n \"Model 2 might be read as submaximal work, but depth-jump item 2\",\n \"Inference: Model 2 might be read as submaximal work, but depth-jump item 2\")\nrep('heuristic--strength-endurance-load-tempo-and-the-75-80-percent-ceiling.md',\n \"(60% of the time to failure is the plain reading)\",\n \"(Inference: 60% of the time to failure is the plain reading)\")\nrep('heuristic--plyometric-training-coupling-under-0-15-s-feedforward-and-force-time-pattern.md',\n \"and dates the earliest published use of \\\"plyometrics\\\" to a Soviet publication (Zanon, 1966).\",\n \"and writes that \\\"The earliest published use of the word plyometrics seems to have been in a Soviet publication (Zanon, 1966).\\\"\")\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\ncd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint && ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky > /tmp/lint5b.txt; grep -c -F -f staging/_scope_supertraining_ch5b.txt /tmp/lint5b.txt; tail -1 /tmp/lint5b.txt; bash -c 'cd staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky; while read -r f; do sed -E \"s/^\\*\\*[^*]+\\*\\* —//\" \"$f\" | grep -c \"—\" ; done < ../../../_scope_supertraining_ch5b.txt | sort | uniq -c; for f in $(cat ../../../_scope_supertraining_ch5b.txt); do grep -m1 \"^kind:\" $f; done | sort | uniq -c; for f in $(cat ../../../_scope_supertraining_ch5b.txt); do grep -m1 \"^confidence:\" $f; done | sort | uniq -c; grep -l \"confidence: contested\" $(cat ../../../_scope_supertraining_ch5b.txt)'","description":"Apply four fixes, rerun lint and tallies"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cffb1Fufj3L4XSGCvbyNn","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"a